## What variant of Codex are you using?

CLI, but this is really an account-level usage feature that would benefit CLI, App, IDE Extension, and Web users.

## What feature would you like to see?

Please allow unused normal Codex quota to roll over into a temporary bank instead of disappearing at the next automatic reset.

For example, if I have 50% of my Codex quota left and my normal reset happens tomorrow, I would like to save that unused 50% for later rather than losing it when the new cycle starts.

A safe version of this could be capped and time-limited, for example:

- unused quota rolls into a temporary bank;
- the bank is capped at 1 extra reset, or some fixed percentage such as 100% of one normal cycle;
- banked quota expires after 7–30 days;
- normal scheduled resets still happen as usual;
- manually granted/banked reset tokens remain separate from unused quota rollover.

This would make Codex much more useful for users whose workload is bursty. Some days I do not need the full quota, while on other days I need a much heavier Codex session. Right now, unused quota before a normal reset feels wasted even when I know I will need it soon.

## Additional information

I understand why unlimited rollover could be hard for capacity planning and abuse prevention. I am not asking for infinite quota hoarding. A small capped rollover would be enough.

Suggested behavior:

- if a user has unused quota at reset time, move part of it into a temporary bank;
- use current-cycle quota first;
- use rolled-over quota only after current-cycle quota is exhausted;
- clearly show the banked amount and expiration date in the usage UI;
- make the feature work for CLI users too, even if the UI lives in the Codex app/web settings.

This would be especially helpful for Pro/Plus users who use Codex heavily but unevenly across days.

## Summary

Makes plugin details/read flows capability-aware so auth-filtered plugin surfaces report the same usable app/MCP/skill shape as the marketplace and install flows.

## Validation

Not run; this change was rebased onto the current plugin auth stack and pushed as a draft PR.

**Manual test**
1. set up a local marketplace with a plugin that has both app and mcp declarations

```
// .app.json
{
  "apps": {
    "linear": {
      "id": "some_id"
    }
  }
}

```

```
// .mcp.json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "linear": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.linear.app/mcp",
      "oauth_resource": "https://mcp.linear.app/mcp"
    },
    "linear2": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.linear2.app/mcp",
      "oauth_resource": "https://mcp.linear2.app/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

2a. **login in with api key** and observe plugin details page which shows no apps (note we don't show "app not available due to api key log in as there's no way to differentiate between no apps and app without substitute mcp exists" without significantly more code changes, i've separated this to a follow up if we want that behaviour.
